 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.3,
   "text": "What would Earth's climate be like if the land masses were rotated by 90 degrees?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.149,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 3.92,
   "end": 5.3,
   "text": "Where would the deserts and forests be?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.149,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 5.6,
   "end": 8.2,
   "text": "And where would you go for a sunny beach vacation or to chase a tornado?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.149,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 8.86,
   "end": 12.1,
   "text": "The main driver of our weather and climate is the sun, which delivers more heat at the",
   "avg_logprob": -0.149,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 12.1,
   "end": 13.24,
   "text": "equator than at the poles.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.149,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 13.68,
   "end": 17.88,
   "text": "So hot air rises at the equator and flows poleward over our heads, then cooler air",
   "avg_logprob": -0.149,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 17.88,
   "end": 19.88,
   "text": "moves in across the surface toward the equator.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.149,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 20.18,
   "end": 21.84,
   "text": "This circulation is called a Hadley cell.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.149,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 22.16,
   "end": 25.78,
   "text": "For various complicated reasons, Earth doesn't have just a single atmospheric cell in each",
   "avg_logprob": -0.149,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 25.78,
   "end": 27.04,
   "text": "hemisphere, we actually have three.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.149,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 27.44,
   "end": 29.38,
   "text": "Hadley cells, ferrule cells, and polar cells.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.149,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 29.9,
   "end": 32.64,
   "text": "Let's assume our rotated world has the same situation going on.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.007
  },
  {
   "start": 32.92,
   "end": 35.34,
   "text": "This means it would have temperature extremes which are similar to ours.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.007
  },
  {
   "start": 35.8,
   "end": 37.68,
   "text": "Here's what a map of our rotator Earth looks like.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.007
  },
  {
   "start": 38.04,
   "end": 41.24,
   "text": "We'll add some ice and permafrost near the poles and in mountainous areas.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.007
  },
  {
   "start": 41.64,
   "end": 43.52,
   "text": "Next, we should fill in some green areas and deserts.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.007
  },
  {
   "start": 44.02,
   "end": 47.34,
   "text": "The locations of these depend heavily on rainfall, so we'll need to sketch out",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.007
  },
  {
   "start": 47.34,
   "end": 47.78,
   "text": "some winds.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.007
  },
  {
   "start": 48.32,
   "end": 51.28,
   "text": "Because of the Coriolis effect, the surface winds in a Hadley cell flow not",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.007
  },
  {
   "start": 51.28,
   "end": 53.28,
   "text": "just toward the equator, but from east to west.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.007
  },
  {
   "start": 53.6,
   "end": 56.72,
   "text": "In the temperate zones, the prevailing surface winds are west to east, and",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.007
  },
  {
   "start": 56.72,
   "end": 59.52,
   "text": "at times there are also east to west winds circulating around the poles.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.116,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.039
  },
  {
   "start": 60.16,
   "end": 63.02,
   "text": "So let's fill in some wind patterns, keeping in mind that in reality, things",
   "avg_logprob": -0.116,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.039
  },
  {
   "start": 63.02,
   "end": 65.98,
   "text": "would be further complicated by land interactions and the locations of",
   "avg_logprob": -0.116,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.039
  },
  {
   "start": 65.98,
   "end": 67.56,
   "text": "persistent high and low pressure systems.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.116,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.039
  },
  {
   "start": 68.06,
   "end": 70.58,
   "text": "The rising air at the equator carries moisture from the ocean, which then",
   "avg_logprob": -0.116,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.039
  },
  {
   "start": 70.58,
   "end": 71.54,
   "text": "condenses into rain.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.116,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.039
  },
  {
   "start": 71.88,
   "end": 74.24,
   "text": "So tropical areas are usually wet and thick with growth.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.116,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.039
  },
  {
   "start": 74.8,
   "end": 77.8,
   "text": "Sinking air is cool and dry, so the land under the outer edges of the",
   "avg_logprob": -0.116,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.039
  },
  {
   "start": 77.8,
   "end": 79.28,
   "text": "Hadley cells tends to be arid.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.116,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.039
  },
  {
   "start": 79.6,
   "end": 82.46,
   "text": "These regions, lying a bit poleward of 30 degrees, are known as the",
   "avg_logprob": -0.116,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.039
  },
  {
   "start": 82.46,
   "end": 83.96,
   "text": "horse latitudes for some reason.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.116,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.039
  },
  {
   "start": 83.96,
   "end": 87.24,
   "text": "In temperate zones, things are more variable, since feral cells aren't as",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.054
  },
  {
   "start": 87.24,
   "end": 88.12,
   "text": "strong as Hadley cells.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.054
  },
  {
   "start": 88.54,
   "end": 91.18,
   "text": "Whether there is dominated instead by the movement of jet streams and",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.054
  },
  {
   "start": 91.18,
   "end": 93.2,
   "text": "fronts, and it also depends heavily on geography.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.054
  },
  {
   "start": 93.9,
   "end": 96.46,
   "text": "Just for fun, here's a wild guess as to where the hurricane basins",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.054
  },
  {
   "start": 96.46,
   "end": 99.54,
   "text": "might be, and for more fun, here's a guess about what time zones",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.054
  },
  {
   "start": 99.54,
   "end": 100.22,
   "text": "would look like.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.054
  },
  {
   "start": 100.66,
   "end": 103.74,
   "text": "New York City, notably, stays in the same time zone and is still",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.054
  },
  {
   "start": 103.74,
   "end": 104.66,
   "text": "subject to hurricanes.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.054
  },
  {
   "start": 105.44,
   "end": 105.5,
   "text": "Sorry.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.151,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.054
  }
 ],
